content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "name, description, tools, maxTurns lead the frontmatter before type/id; principle sets, reconcile-and-close, and glossary terms are referenced not embedded; no actor kind committed; the unset cost threshold is handled in-file (\"until set, every such commitment escalates\")"}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "No sentence says when the seat acts or what step precedes/follows it; Interfaces describe flows (arrives/returns), not ordering"}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "Exactly one exclusive claim: \"the stack — which technologies the product is built on is decided by this seat alone\"; decision-phrased"}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Six bullets, each an artifact or judgment checkable after a run (structural model, ADRs, decomposition record, scenario map, reconciliation via registers, screened decisions with escalated exceptions); no trait bullets"}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "maxTurns 60 caps a drift-prone write-capable seat; the 'never from its internals' stance has no frontmatter key that could enforce it (tools can't scope paths), so it is a standard of evidence rather than an enforceable-but-unenforced claim"}
stumbles: ["\"pre-state determines the vehicle — what a Bounded Context actually is before a change ... decides which message type a request travels in\" — one long sentence carrying a definition and a rule; reads twice", "\"any stack decision that commits the product to a vendor or a recurring cost above the threshold the authority sets when it approves this seat — until set, every such commitment escalates\" — the escalate bullet is the only one whose rule depends on an external act; fine, but dense"]
top_changes: ["Split the posture's first sentence: state the pre-state definition (a link to the glossary suffices) separately from the rule that it selects the vehicle", "Optionally add a short note beside the tools key that reading Bounded Context internals is out of scope by standard of evidence, not by tool restriction, so a future reviewer does not re-open scenario 5 on it"]
